    "data": {
      "title": "Change Trace",
      "topics": [],
      "fastest": true,
      "reverse": false,
      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int amount, n;\n    int last_coin[101];\n    scanf(\"%d %d\", &amount, &n);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        scanf(\"%d\", &last_coin[i]);\n    }\n\n    if (amount == 0) {\n        puts(\"NONE\");\n    } else if (last_coin[amount] == -1) {\n        puts(\"IMPOSSIBLE\");\n    } else {\n        int first = 1;\n        while (amount > 0) {\n            int coin = last_coin[amount];\n            printf(\"%s%d\", first ? \"\" : \" \", coin);\n            first = 0;\n            amount -= coin;\n        }\n        putchar('\\n');\n    }\n    return 0;\n}",
      "statement": "The minimum-change table is already computed. At index [[v]], [[lastCoin]] contains the value of the last coin chosen for amount [[v]], or {{-1}} if it is impossible.\n\nStarting at [[amount]], take that coin and subtract its value. Repeat until {{0}}. Print the coins in this traversal order, {{IMPOSSIBLE}} for impossible change, or {{NONE}} for amount {{0}}.",
